      Direction","comment":null,"color":{"r":0.4745098,"g":0.8784314,"b":0.8901961,"a":1.0},"guid":"aebe6105-66df-4b99-ae69-5c67ffa374d1","$version":"A","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.GraphGroup"},{"position":{"xMin":-643.0,"yMin":301.0,"xMax":1915.185,"yMax":1001.0},"label":"Hurt","comment":null,"color":{"r":1.0,"g":0.5019608,"b":0.5019608,"a":1.0},"guid":"3b195609-bcbe-4f9e-bbbf-727c20931b13","$version":"A","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.GraphGroup"},{"position":{"xMin":-406.0,"yMin":735.0,"xMax":-247.0,"yMax":831.0},"title":"Hurt","body":"Triggered
      by things that deal damage. Changes health by the given damage and flashes.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"d41deb50-afff-418c-bb08-b3a6a80e8d3f","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3073.0,"yMin":407.0,"xMax":-2859.0,"yMax":497.0},"title":"Animation
      Direction","body":"A little bit of logic that flips the character around (using
      negative scale) and stores the current facing direction.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"115267cd-3221-424c-a870-13e489e52ce2","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3559.0,"yMin":1246.0,"xMax":-3397.667,"yMax":1324.0},"title":"AI
      Enemy","body":"Script for doing enemy things that aren''t state dependent.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"456cc0e8-f783-415f-b87f-4d1f24febcd7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3218.0,"yMin":1634.0,"xMax":-3017.0,"yMax":1744.0},"title":"AI
      Enemy","body":"Permanently stop the enemy from using the Z-axis (which would
      allow it to walk around the player) by constantly moving it to 0 on the Z-axis","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"93f276f7-0eff-4887-9975-c415845b4122","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-2691.0,"yMin":896.0,"xMax":-2436.0,"yMax":978.0},"title":"Animation
      Direction","body":"Only set the animation direction variable if the actual
      direction is not 0 (i.e. the enemy isn''t standing still).","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"faa110d3-369a-4b7e-a54b-7a30ffc8359d","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-2107.0,"yMin":402.0,"xMax":-1842.0,"yMax":507.0},"title":"Animation
      Direction","body":"Multiply the absolute value of the local scale on the x-axis
      by the direction, which makes it face left with negative scale on negative
      direction and right with positive scale on positive direction.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"79e4871b-ad4e-4bf1-b2a2-f1bfce231552","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-1895.0,"yMin":912.0,"xMax":-1723.0,"yMax":980.0},"title":"Animation
      Direction","body":"Only apply the flip if the enemy is not attacking.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"11bf7d62-7ab9-4465-9a2b-e674001ce9e4","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":438.0,"yMin":880.0,"xMax":568.0,"yMax":958.0},"title":"Hurt","body":"Play
      the enemy hurt sound for player feedback.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"7a78b792-8b69-4497-9945-e3b4c0bed340","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":1276.0,"yMin":887.0,"xMax":1450.0,"yMax":964.0},"title":"Hurt","body":"If
